{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_3y5msjmacuvpjcqgxrnkgjsvhipq7kspuzqq3uokmy3y2xzofwka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both debug and release builds compile cleanly. The implementation:\n\n**Translation summary:**\n\n1. **`compute_indexes`**: Mirrors the C helper that determines byte indexes for the LSB and MSB plus the bit offset within the LSB byte. For MOTOROLA (big-endian DBC bit numbering) it walks down `len-1` bits, jumping from bit_0 of one byte to bit_7 of the next byte. For INTEL, it directly computes `msb = startbit + len - 1`.\n\n2. **`frame_to_local`**: Builds an 8-byte little-endian buffer containing the signal-bearing chunk. For MOTOROLA the bytes are reverse-copied (LSB byte first, then bytes leading toward the MSB). For INTEL, simple sequential copy.\n\n3. **`extract`**: Loads the chunk, right-shifts by `offset_lsb`, masks to `len` bits, then sign-extends if `signedness == SIGNED` and the MSB is set.\n\n4. **`insert`**: Mirrors `extract` but writes back. The signal bits are masked to `len` first to mimic C truncation when shifting a wider value into a narrow field, then OR'd into the chunk and written back to the frame respecting endianness.\n\n5. **Encode/decode wrappers**: Match the original C casting semantics (computing in `f64`, casting via `i64` for signed paths so negative values reinterpret correctly into `u64`).\n\n6. **Edge cases**: `make_mask` handles `len == 64` (avoids the C-style undefined behavior of `1 << 64`); the indexing loops are bounded by 8 bytes to keep the implementation fully safe Rust without `unsafe` or FFI."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":261,"cache_read_input_tokens":44541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":261,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id"